## §11 — Rollback (if smoke fails)

If the smoke fails, **the bug is in a SKILL.md**, not in the graduated
code. Revert the graduation, fix the SKILL.md, delete the sandbox,
re-invoke `compose-domain`, re-graduate.

```bash
# Rollback every diff this GRADUATION.md prescribed and remove every
# copied file. Run from repo root, immediately after a graduation commit.
git restore --source=HEAD~1 \
    function_app.py \
    api/functions/graphs/__init__.py \
    api/server/services/simulator_orchestrator.py \
    api/server/routes/simulator.py \
    api/server/services/blueprint_inventory.py \
    api/shared/constants.py
rm -rf \
    api/server/skills/{{DOMAIN_NAME}}-* \
    api/server/personae/{{PERSONA_ROLES_GLOB}} \
{{REMOVE_TOOL_FILES}} \
    api/functions/workflows/{{DOMAIN_NAME_SNAKE}}.py \
    api/functions/workflows/{{DOMAIN_NAME_SNAKE}}_activities.py \
    api/functions/graphs/{{DOMAIN_NAME_SNAKE}}_*.py \
    api/functions/graphs/executors/agents/agent_{{DOMAIN_NAME_SNAKE}}_*.py \
    api/functions/graphs/executors/validators/validate_{{DOMAIN_NAME_SNAKE}}_*.py
```

If graduation has not yet been committed, replace `git restore` with
`git checkout --` against the working tree.
